<body>
<header><h1>🖥️ Generations of Computers</h1><p>Explore how computer technology developed.</p></header>
<main>
<article class="card"><span class="period">First Generation</span><h2>Vacuum Tubes</h2><p>Early electronic computers used vacuum tubes. They were large, expensive and produced considerable heat.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="period">Second Generation</span><h2>Transistors</h2><p>Transistors replaced vacuum tubes in many computer designs, helping computers become smaller and more reliable.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="period">Third Generation</span><h2>Integrated Circuits</h2><p>Integrated circuits placed multiple electronic components on a small chip.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="period">Fourth Generation</span><h2>Microprocessors</h2><p>Microprocessors helped make personal computers widely available.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="period">Fifth Generation</span><h2>Artificial Intelligence</h2><p>This commonly used educational category highlights AI, advanced processing and intelligent computing systems.</p></article>
</main>
